<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Padding @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>

<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-padding-*</span> CSS classes: the utility classes provided, the strongly-typed <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Padding</span> C# object
    used to apply them, and the supporting enum used to select a spacing value.
</p>

<h2 class="page-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Padding</span> is a <b>utility class</b>, not a BEM component class like <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Section</span> or <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Button</span>.
    Rather than describing a block, element, or its variants, each class here sets a single CSS property to a fixed value from the shared <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-space-*</span>
    spacing scale. Utility classes are flat and single-purpose by design, so they can be freely combined with each other and with any other class - including component classes - on the same element.
</p>
<p>
    Because they read directly from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-space-*</span> primitives - values that rarely change once a theme is set - these classes are not
    part of the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-cls-*</span> theme-reactive colour layer described on other pages.
</p>

<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="page-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Padding</span> provides utility classes that set padding from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-space-*</span> primitive scale.
    </p>
    <section class="code-table">
